**Locating the Definition**

I'm now zeroing in on where the "AI Playground" exhibit is defined within the codebase. Initial investigation suggests the file structure holds the key, and I will be looking where the content is rendered.


**Pinpointing the Components**

I've located the "AI Playground" definition within `constants.tsx`, specifically under the `stanford-ai` category as `ai-playground`. Rendering logic is spread across `App.tsx` and `components/ExhibitDetail.tsx`. I've verified that the `ExhibitDetail` component corresponds to the "AI Playground" page as per the user's screenshot.


**Adding the New Link**

I'm inserting the SLS guide link within the `constants.tsx` file, under the `ai-playground` entry within `EXHIBIT_CATEGORIES`. The new link will sit right next to the existing link to launch the AI playground. I've also reconfirmed that the `ExhibitDetail` component will render the new link correctly, as the link array is being iterated over.


**Confirming the Rendering**

I've examined the rendering logic within `ExhibitDetail.tsx` more closely. I can see that the component iterates through the `item.links` array in the `EXHIBIT_CATEGORIES` constant, and renders a button for each link. The code uses `href={link.url}` to set the link's URL. The new SLS Guide link will therefore render a button correctly. The `constants.tsx` file now contains the new link.


**Adding the Second Link**

I'm now adding the new link, `https://sites.google.com/law.stanford.edu/ailearninghub/sls-training-center/stanford-ai-playground`, to the `constants.tsx` file, specifically the `ai-playground` item's `links` array. I confirm this will result in a second, red button appearing next to the existing "Launch AI Playground" button. The button's appearance will mirror the existing link's style, based on my understanding of the `ExhibitDetail` component's rendering logic.


**Verifying the Placement**

I've decided on "SLS Guide" as the link title. I am now adding the new link to the `constants.tsx` file, right next to the existing "Launch AI Playground" link. The rendering logic within `ExhibitDetail.tsx` utilizes `flex-wrap gap-4`, which is good to see. This confirms the new link will appear as a button alongside the existing one, with the correct spacing, as designed.


**Considering the Visuals**

